# Markdown: code blocks between fences and indented, styled with For element: Code block.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Markdown · Code blocks
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Code block
			Typography:
				Size: 9
				Line height: 13
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 10 0
				Padding: 8 10
				Background: sand
				Corner radius: 4
	Section:
		Text: Markdown
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Code blocks
		Paragraph: A block between three backticks or three tildes, or indented four spaces, is a `Code block`: preformatted text in the `Code font`. It has no look of its own, `For element: Code block` gives it the background and the padding. A language tag after the fence is an error.
			Style: intro
		Markdown:
			Content >>
				Between backticks:

				```
				$ thermostat --status
				temperature   21.5 °C
				setpoint      22.0 °C
				```

				Between tildes:

				~~~
				Reference: 2026-014
				~~~

				Indented four spaces:

				    mvn -o test
				    mvn -o package
